*> Shulker boxes (docs/protocol/52 section 4, 31-1 section 13): the client keeps the shulker boxes of the loaded chunks (SB-BOX; found when a chunk loads (SHULKER-SCAN), when a block
*> changes (WORLD-BLOCK-SET: SHULKER-NOTE) and forgotten with the chunk or the dimension), their colour (the block's name), facing (the state's property) and the lid animation: Block Event 1
*> with the parameter 1 opens, 0 closes (13.3), a client tick steps the lid by a tenth (ticks 0 to 10, 13.2: the status flips on the tenth tick), a parameter of 2 or more changes nothing.
*> SHULKER-MESH draws the lid and the base (the model of 4.2, the transform of 4.3, the lid at (0, 24 - 8 p, 0) turned p x 270 degrees about Y, 4.4) into the entity mesh with the entity atlas slot
*> of the colour's texture. Expected corners from an independent script (scratchpad/models/shulker_box.py, written from the document text) for six boxes (facing up closed, east half open,
*> down open, north at a third, south and west).
